  "exact_main_statement": "For every k : Nat, ((k : Real)+12)^(k+11) <= 3^12*12^11*6144^k*(k.factorial : Real).",
  "proof_points": [
    "For x=k+12>=0, the kth nonnegative exponential-series term gives x^k/k!<=exp(x); exp(1)<3 and exp(n)=exp(1)^n imply x^k<=3^(k+12)*k!.",
    "Induction proves k+1<=2^k, hence k+12<=12*2^k. Raising to the eleventh power is monotone on nonnegative reals.",
    "Multiplication combines the two powers; 3*2^11=6144 exactly. The argument applies to k=0 without division by k or asymptotic estimates."
  ],
  "scope": "Unconditional scalar arithmetic only. No analytic recurrence, Sobolev embedding, physical derivative estimate, approximation theorem, executable solver or complexity statement is asserted. The 6144 constant is sufficient, not claimed optimal.",
